  "summary": "Package exfiltrates host identifiers and full process.env to Burp Collaborator on require",
  "details": "index.js runs on require() and collects os.hostname(), os.arch(), os.userInfo().username, the install path, and both the keys and values of process.env, then issues an HTTPS GET to the hardcoded host zuxsp9k9vyk5y45z1n2hv0orhin9b2zr.oastify.com (Burp Collaborator out-of-band domain). Environment values commonly include CI tokens, cloud credentials, and npm publish tokens, all of which leave the installer's machine to an attacker-controlled destination on module load.",
